From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaosen <0x5e@sina.cn>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:25:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(bt): pair as an accessory with no display or keypad

Registered as `KeyboardDisplay`, this made the phone put a six-digit number on
its screen and wait for someone to confirm it. There is no display here to show
that number on, so the operator's only part in the pairing was tapping a figure
the board never saw. `NoInputNoOutput` describes the same accessory honestly:
the link comes up as just works, with nothing on the phone to tap.
---

diff --git a/native/crates/livi-runtime/src/bt.rs b/native/crates/livi-runtime/src/bt.rs
--- a/native/crates/livi-runtime/src/bt.rs
+++ b/native/crates/livi-runtime/src/bt.rs
@@ -304,12 +304,18 @@
         start_carplay(&conn, adapter, tx).await?;
     }
 
+    // Pairs as an accessory with neither a display nor a keypad, which is what
+    // this is: claiming `KeyboardDisplay` made the phone put a six-digit number
+    // on its screen and wait for a confirmation nobody here can give — the
+    // board has no display to show the number it would be confirming. With
+    // `NoInputNoOutput` the same pairing completes as just works, and the phone
+    // shows nothing to tap.
     conn.call_method(
         Some("org.bluez"),
         "/org/bluez",
         Some("org.bluez.AgentManager1"),
         "RegisterAgent",
-        &(ObjectPath::try_from(AGENT_PATH)?, "KeyboardDisplay"),
+        &(ObjectPath::try_from(AGENT_PATH)?, "NoInputNoOutput"),
     )
     .await?;
     conn.call_method(
